config-connector-extensions patch 0061: a hierarchical firewall policy's
addRule adds the rule to the policy's rules.

FirewallPoliciesV1.AddRule replaced the policy's rules with the one added,
so adding a second rule removed the first (and the default rules the
policy is made with). It now appends the rule, as
NetworkFirewallPoliciesV1.AddRule does, for ComputeFirewallPolicyRule
(ours; foundation item 19), whose test makes two rules in one policy.
Upstream candidate: yes.

--- a/mockgcp/mockcompute/firewallpoliciesv1.go
+++ b/mockgcp/mockcompute/firewallpoliciesv1.go
@@ -199,7 +199,10 @@
 	r := req.GetFirewallPolicyRuleResource()
 	mockFieldValuesForRule(r)
 
-	obj.Rules = []*pb.FirewallPolicyRule{r}
+	// A rule is added to the policy's rules, as the network policy's
+	// addRule does; it replaced them all, so a second rule removed the
+	// first and the default rules.
+	obj.Rules = append(obj.Rules, r)
 	if err := s.storage.Update(ctx, fqn, obj); err != nil {
 		return nil, err
 	}
